The lead-acid battery market continues to serve important automotive, industrial, and energy backup applications. Its established manufacturing base, relatively low upfront cost, high surge-current capability, and extensive recycling infrastructure support continued use despite growing competition from lithium-ion and other advanced battery technologies.

What Is the Lead-Acid Battery Market?
The lead-acid battery market covers rechargeable battery systems that store and release electrical energy through an electrochemical reaction involving lead and sulfuric acid. These batteries are widely used in automotive starting systems, motorcycles, forklifts, uninterruptible power supplies, telecommunications infrastructure, and stationary backup applications.

